{
 "lines": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.2,
   "text": "Delete Obsidian because Cloud just solved its biggest problem and built itself a second"
  },
  {
   "start": 3.2,
   "end": 3.5,
   "text": "brain."
  },
  {
   "start": 3.74,
   "end": 6.92,
   "text": "This is insane because it now automatically remembers your projects and preferences across"
  },
  {
   "start": 6.92,
   "end": 7.9,
   "text": "every single conversation."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.24,
   "end": 11.0,
   "text": "If you use Cloud, you know how annoying it is when it keeps forgetting important details"
  },
  {
   "start": 11.0,
   "end": 12.0,
   "text": "every time you switch chats."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.16,
   "end": 14.1,
   "text": "Now, Cloud saves details dynamically in the background."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.32,
   "end": 17.2,
   "text": "So you can go into your settings and literally see your memories categorized by topic."
  },
  {
   "start": 17.44,
   "end": 20.36,
   "text": "You can click on any file to edit the details or delete anything you want it to forget."
  },
  {
   "start": 20.58,
   "end": 24.92,
   "text": "Even it even works in your browser across the desktop app and even on mobile for all"
  },
  {
   "start": 24.92,
   "end": 25.26,
   "text": "users."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.48,
   "end": 28.36,
   "text": "Now this completely changes how you use Cloud, but there's one major catch you need to"
  },
  {
   "start": 28.36,
   "end": 29.24,
   "text": "know before you turn this on."
  },
  {
   "start": 29.24,
   "end": 32.34,
   "text": "If you set your tasks to run locally on your machine, the memory won't sync because it"
  },
  {
   "start": 32.34,
   "end": 33.14,
   "text": "only works in the cloud."
  },
  {
   "start": 33.32,
   "end": 34.4,
   "text": "Comment mem for the free setup."
  }
 ],
